  "tagline": "Serverless single-file NoSQL document database for .NET, in the spirit of SQLite.",
  "description": "LiteDB is an embedded document database written in C# that stores BSON documents in a single file. It offers ACID transactions, a write-ahead log, indexes on any expression, LINQ and a SQL-like query syntax, and optional AES encryption. It is the usual pick when a .NET desktop, tool or small service wants document storage without a native SQLite dependency or a separate server. The stable 5.0 line has not had a release since mid-2024, while a 6.0 rewrite has been in public prerelease and active development through 2026.",
